[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495870214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99115#issuecomment-2495870214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99115","id":2495870214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uw_UG","user":{"login":"ImamuraCross","id":187475975,"node_id":"U_kgDOCyyoBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/187475975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross","html_url":"https://github.com/ImamuraCross","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImamuraCross/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-24T08:27:57Z","updated_at":"2024-11-24T08:27:57Z","body":"Issue still exists as of **v4.4.dev5.official [9e6098432]**; post edited to reflect further testing.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2495870214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2655431651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99115#issuecomment-2655431651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99115","id":2655431651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eRqvj","user":{"login":"robcbryant","id":25797518,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1Nzk3NTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25797518?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant","html_url":"https://github.com/robcbryant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robcbryant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T04:10:35Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T06:22:18Z","body":"I can confirm this is an issue in v4.4.beta3.official [06acfccf8]  as well -- In my case I'm trying to edit a Sprites \"Frame Coords\" with the path \"PlayerSprite.frame_coords:x\"   in the AnimationPlayer and it still forces a Vector2.  It's a pretty big issue for me in terms of how I'm animating sprites--and has broken several older animation sets for various enemies.\n\nIs there a spot in the codebase I could investigate to look into trying to see the issue?\n\nEDIT:\n\n\n\n\n>tracks/2/type = \"value\"\ntracks/2/imported = false\ntracks/2/enabled = true\ntracks/2/path = NodePath(\"PlayerSprite:frame_coords:x\")\ntracks/2/interp = 1\ntracks/2/loop_wrap = false\ntracks/2/keys = {\n\"times\": PackedFloat32Array(0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8),\n\"transitions\": PackedFloat32Array(1, 1, 1, 1, 1),\n\"update\": 1,\n\"values\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n}\n\n\nI can confirm in the raw scene file that it's original stored values are in fact--floats and not vector2s, but while running the game in the editor--it randomly seems to pull the arbitrary y value of \"0\" from thin air, when it changes animations.\n\n\nUPDATE:\n\nI found a way to brute force a solution that's messy but will work for now but is a little inelegant. Essentially in a _process() function on the AnimationPlayer I brute force the frame_coord.y value to the desired value every frame which overwrites whatever phantom value the Animation Player is pulling from these Vector2 values rather than the needed float value.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2655431651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2804485657","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99115#issuecomment-2804485657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99115","id":2804485657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nKQ4Z","user":{"login":"tannineo","id":33346345,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzQ2MzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33346345?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo","html_url":"https://github.com/tannineo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tannineo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/us